  "result": "Perfect! All 106 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT calculation to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Added `lineVat(line)` function that:\n  - Calculates VAT on the line amount after discount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n  - Rounds each line's VAT independently using `roundCents()`\n  - Clamps result to minimum 0\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where:\n  - `vat` = sum of all individual rounded line VATs\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat\n  - All amounts clamped to minimum 0\n\n**Changes to `src/render.js`:**\n- Imports `lineVat` function\n- Shows VAT line before total when VAT > 0:\n  - Format: `VAT: \u20acamount` (using `formatEuros()`)\n  - Only shown if there's actually VAT to display\n\n**Key Design:**\n- VAT is per-line and rounded independently, not a percentage of invoice total\n- Invoice VAT = sum of all separately-rounded line VATs\n- This ensures accurate accounting per tax jurisdiction requirements\n\n**Tests:** 106 total\n- 10 new tests for `lineVat()` covering multiple VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%), discount interactions, and rounding\n- 3 new tests for `invoiceTotals()` with VAT including mixed VAT rates\n- 4 new tests for render output showing VAT line\n- Updated 14 existing tests to account for VAT in calculations\n\nAll 106 tests pass. \u2705",
